Press <kbd>{{$:/config/shortcuts/py-quick-capture}}</kbd> from anywhere in your wiki to open the ''Quick Capture'' modal (you can customize this shortcut in [[Control Panel > Keyboard Shortcuts|$:/core/ui/ControlPanel/KeyboardShortcuts]]).

!! Smart Inline Tokens

All task inputs in Projectify—including Quick Capture, the Inbox input, Project task forms, and inline sub-task inputs—support natural inline tokens when ''Smart Quick Add'' is enabled:

|!Token |!Effect |!Example |
|`!1`, `!2`, `!3` or `p1`–`p3` |Sets task priority (`1` = Low, `2` = Medium, `3` = High) |`Fix login bug !3` |
|`@today`, `@tomorrow`, `@nextweek`, `@YYYY-MM-DD` |Sets the ''Due Date'' (`due`) |`Submit tax forms @2026-04-15` |
|`~today`, `~tomorrow`, `~nextweek`, `~YYYY-MM-DD` |Sets the ''Start / Scheduled Date'' (`scheduled`) |`Draft proposal ~tomorrow` |
|`#Project` or `#[Project Name]` |Files the task directly into an existing project (instead of Inbox) |`Buy plane tickets #[Book vacation trip]` |
|`@context` (e.g. `@work`, `@home`, `@calls`) |Adds one or more `@context` tags to the task |`Call dentist @calls @errands` |

You can also use the ''Project dropdown'', ''Schedule'', and ''Priority'' pickers directly inside the Quick Capture modal.
